  "callouts": [
    {
      "id": "note-loop",
      "kind": "note",
      "text": "refine() → smooth() → back into refine(): a loop's back edge drawn between two Blocks, because the Loop region does not exist yet. The back cable is already marked delayed.",
      "x": 120,
      "y": 80,
      "w": 520,
      "h": 150
    },
    {
      "id": "step-1",
      "kind": "step",
      "text": "1 · Click the dotted cable from smooth.pose back into refine.pose. In the inspector, Temporal reads Delayed (z⁻¹).",
      "x": 700,
      "y": 80,
      "w": 380,
      "h": 140,
      "target": {
        "shapeId": "smooth",
        "anchor": "top",
        "dx": -40
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-2",
      "kind": "step",
      "text": "2 · Type 1.0 in the inspector's = value field and press Enter. The pill reads z⁻¹ = 1.0.",
      "x": 1130,
      "y": 80,
      "w": 380,
      "h": 140
    },
    {
      "id": "step-3",
      "kind": "step",
      "text": "3 · Drag the pill along the cable, then click Centre the pill in the inspector.",
      "x": 120,
      "y": 880,
      "w": 420,
      "h": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "step-4",
      "kind": "step",
      "text": "4 · Open the Dev Hub (</> bottom right) and switch on \"Solid before the z⁻¹ pill\": the run into the pill turns solid and the run after it stays dotted. Mark the seed cable (estimate → refine) delayed too, via right-click › Delayed (z⁻¹), and compare.",
      "x": 980,
      "y": 610,
      "w": 520,
      "h": 180
    },
    {
      "id": "pass",
      "kind": "pass",
      "text": "PASS WHEN the back cable is dotted with a z⁻¹ pill you can slide, the pill shows = 1.0 after step 2, the Dev Hub switch makes only the run before the pill solid, and a reload keeps all of it.",
